Why Notchy as a whole is GPL v3
-------------------------------

Notchy incorporates code derived from Atoll (https://github.com/Ebullioscopic/Atoll),
which is licensed under the GNU General Public License v3.0 and which itself
derives from boring.notch. The GPL v3 requires that the combined work be
distributed under the GPL v3, so that is the licence of Notchy as a whole.

MIT permits this: Coucou's code may be incorporated into a GPL v3 work provided
its copyright and permission notice travel with it, which is the purpose of the
notice above. Coucou's original code remains available under the MIT licence
from its own repository; nothing here restricts it there.

A practical consequence, recorded deliberately: Coucou ships a Mac App Store
build, and Notchy cannot. GPL v3 and the App Store's distribution terms are
incompatible, so the CoucouAppStore target was removed rather than left to fail
later.

